#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:5
#: d0ba5e3b7b914f68903f900b34d73a1c
msgid "Land Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:7
#: 4593bf0f976d45e3a125db6565621d18
msgid "LAND Mode attempts to bring the copter straight down and has these features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:10
#: 25bd34806e034158b9499ad0ac7e6c30
msgid "descends at :ref:`LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS<LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS>`, if non-zero, (or :ref:`WP_SPD_DN <WP_SPD_DN>` if zero) using the regular Altitude Hold controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:11
#: cbf56efff150447f8bc3d044beade650
msgid "the pilot can reposition the vehicle using the pitch and roll sticks unless the :ref:`LAND_REPOSITION <LAND_REPOSITION>` parameter is changed to \"0\". The throttle stick has no effect by default, although high throttle can cancel landing if enabled via :ref:`PILOT_THR_BHV<PILOT_THR_BHV>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:12
#: df4eb469689947ae8bfe7c64410c978f
msgid "if a rangefinder is being used, or :ref:`TERRAIN_ENABLE<TERRAIN_ENABLE>` =1 and terrain data is available, the descent speed will then switch to :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` at :ref:`LAND_ALT_LOW_M<LAND_ALT_LOW_M>` altitude (default is 10m) above ground until landing occurs. If neither terrain data or rangefinder data is available, then altitude above HOME will be used for the speed switch point (if reached)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:17
#: d2df7b0a4f094f9ab2c25fbd83eb1e91
msgid "below 10m the copter should descend at the rate specified in the :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` parameter which defaults to 50cm/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:23
#: c2420eeab8924536a85b5f3c23608361
msgid "Upon reaching the ground the copter will automatically shut-down the motors and disarm the copter if the pilot's throttle is at minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:28
#: f1a6410c887a4184bac8968bea9c3fb0
msgid "Copter will recognise that it has landed when ALL of the following are true for approximately one second:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:31
#: 4502c0f86bbd42fab8074e7089a31e19
msgid "Motors are commanded to their lower limit by the vertical position controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:32
#: 5107b7a962464fa5aae912be16758760
msgid "Throttle is at minimum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:33
#: ef6c89d7189642ed95b28cad0a835f47
msgid "No large angle is being requested (roll/pitch target < 15°)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:34
#: 3dc4e01fce8846e69b2a802e0d7698df
msgid "No large angle error exists (attitude error < 30°)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:35
#: 26ae31bb13814db0b1fc87c83d419943
msgid "The airframe is not accelerating downward > 1m/s/s ( >2 m/s/s if Weight on Wheels feature is enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:36
#: 65f47900e57843dcafdf90391afec947
msgid "Vertical speed is within 1 m/s of zero ( within 2 m/s if Weight on Wheels feature is enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:37
#: 54a465765e0346a4a71986922c3d6564
msgid "If a healthy rangefinder is available, and rangefinder altitude is below 2m"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:38
#: 291142a5ecab4b03b6b70dcaeb7f15c0
msgid "Weight-on-Wheels (WoW) sensor (if present) confirms contact or is unknown"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:40
#: 1b68f8d13c2e424d8d8f9c2f723c9a7e
msgid "Altitude above home is **not** used as a motor shutoff condition (except when a rangefinder is used,see above). The ``LAND_ALT_LOW_M`` parameter (default 10m) only controls the **descent speed transition** from :ref:`LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS<LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS>` to :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` — it has no role in landing detection or disarming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:45
#: 90ea2b52af7b44f4bf16df39a50ae18c
msgid "For Traditional Heli, the low motor check in the above landing detection algorithm is replaced with a check that Collective output is below mid-position (controlled by the vertical position controller, ie in descent). The rotor still may be at governor speed up until Motor Interlock is removed and  disarming occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:47
#: 6f09d91d40274787bf8a37b0e035785d
msgid "Using a Weight on Wheels (WoW) switch will increase the descent rate and accelerometer ranges that are acceptable for landing detection. This feature is enabled anytime the LGR_WOW_PIN is not disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:52
#: afc05c5eb3a5429fa4ba9925441e2222
msgid "If the copter appears to bounce or balloon back up a couple of times before settling down and turning the props off, try lowering the :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` parameter a bit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:55
#: d1c3a59871c74bbab8d8bc0a5ec82cce
msgid "If the vehicle has GPS lock the landing controller will attempt to control its horizontal position, but the pilot can adjust the target horizontal position just as in Loiter mode, unless the :ref:`LAND_REPOSITION<LAND_REPOSITION>` parameter is set to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:59
#: e5b248867b67424fbdfb5dcf3cc0eba2
msgid "If the vehicle does not have GPS lock the horizontal control will be as in stabilize mode, so the pilot can control the roll and pitch lean angle of the copter, unless the :ref:`LAND_REPOSITION<LAND_REPOSITION>` parameter is set to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:66
#: b34deec1856e466cb0c8ff461cc19792
msgid "In any Alt Hold based mode including: Alt Hold, Loiter, Auto, Auto NAV_Land or RTL if your copters operation becomes erratic when you are close to the ground or landing (and also if any auto landing procedure results in bouncing or failure to turn off motors properly after landing) you probably have the autopilot situated such that its barometer (altimeter) is being affected by the pressure created by the copters prop-wash against the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:76
#: da223eca5c894e3aa12b3709cf62e6be
msgid "This is easily verified by looking at the Altimeter reading in your logs and seeing if it spikes or oscillates when near the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:78
#: 6e53e7de3e1545669513a1c9c63b671d
msgid "If this is a problem, move the autopilot out of prop wash effect or shield it with an appropriately ventilated enclosure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/land-mode.rst:80
#: c777cdf2ab274850910ac2df5e33c9af
msgid "Success can be verified by flight test and by log results."
msgstr ""
